{"author":{"id":"40e3ba2788b3b9fc163c354afc44e5f9d225bcf0a27e679aaa878dd6135c6dcb"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777789761,"nonce":"xe72IyrSDf1GJmf4jpM9pJ8F6eM=","title":"Phase 7: OpenTimestamps integration (anchor archive hash to Bitcoin)","message":"Anchor archive content hash via OpenTimestamps to a Bitcoin block. One HTTP POST to a calendar server returns a pending proof; later upgrade attaches a Bitcoin block-header attestation. Store proof blob as a UC2-OTS trailer (magic-bracketed sidecar appended after EndOfCdir; reverse-scan from EOF). uc2 -t verifies leaf and structural validity; uc2 --ots-attach to attach an externally-acquired .ots; uc2 --ots-extract to dump the proof for the standard 'ots' tool. SHA-256 needed (calendars take SHA-256 of archive content).","files":null}]}